From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:39:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(miniwin): draw immediate mode, viewport rectangles and
 rectangle clears on SDL GPU

Implement SubmitImmediate, SetViewportRect and ClearRect on the SDL3 GPU
backend, with the software backend as the reference.

- Transform, back-face culling, Direct3D lighting and vertex fog run on
  the CPU through immediatemode.cpp, exactly as on the software backend,
  as a DirectX 6 HAL device without hardware T&L had them done. The GPU
  clips and rasterizes the lit triangles.
- New ImmediateVertex/ImmediatePixel shaders take clip-space vertices
  with diffuse and specular colours and apply texture stage 0 (point or
  bilinear, colour-keyed texels discarded), the specular colour and
  vertex or table fog. Colours are interpolated linearly on screen, as
  Gouraud shading was; texture coordinates are perspective-correct.
- Pipelines are created per blend factors and z states. The depth
  buffer holds 1 - z, so that clearing it to 0 is the far plane for
  immediate and retained-mode draws alike (the two encode depth
  differently between the planes, so they do not sort against each
  other within one frame). The viewport is shifted by half a pixel to
  sample where Direct3D's rasterizer does.
- Draws and rectangle clears are recorded and replayed in one render
  pass after a single upload of their vertices; everything else that
  draws flushes them first, so the drawing order is kept, and a
  retained-mode mesh after a flush gets its pipeline and viewport back.
- Textures are keyed (colour key and decal colour) as the software
  backend keys them, for both modes; upstream's retained-mode shaders
  show the decal key only through alpha blending.
- The 'Unsupported number of lights' error is logged once: immediate
  mode lights with every light, and the retained-mode shader's limit of
  three no longer floods the log every frame.

The ImmediateVertex and ImmediatePixel headers were generated with
SDL_shadercross and DXC 1.9.2609 (SPIR-V, DXIL, MSL) and vkd3d-utils 1.17
(DXBC). Retained-mode shaders are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

